WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.519 --> 00:00:03.900
Business continuity refers to enabling the critical

2
00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:07.110
aspects of the organization to function perhaps

3
00:00:07.119 --> 00:00:12.140
at a reduced capacity during a disruption caused by any form of disturbance,

4
00:00:12.149 --> 00:00:15.979
attack, infrastructure failure or natural disaster.

5
00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:20.930
Most incidents are minor and can be handled easily with minimal impact.

6
00:00:21.209 --> 00:00:23.860
A system requires a reboot for example.

7
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:28.139
But after a few minutes, the system is back in operation and the incident is over.

8
00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:29.959
But once in a while,

9
00:00:29.969 --> 00:00:34.099
a major incident will interrupt business for an unacceptable length of time

10
00:00:34.259 --> 00:00:36.889
and the organization cannot just follow an incident

11
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.189
plan but must move toward business continuity.

12
00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.340
Business continuity includes planning,

13
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.840
preparation response and recovery operations,

14
00:00:47.009 --> 00:00:49.979
but it does not generally include activities to support

15
00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.169
full restoration of all business activities and services.

16
00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:56.340
It focuses on the critical products and services

17
00:00:56.349 --> 00:01:00.040
that the organization provides and ensures those important areas

18
00:01:00.049 --> 00:01:02.639
can continue to operate even at a reduced

19
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.949
level of performance until business returns to normal.

20
00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:11.059
Developing a business continuity plan requires a significant organizational

21
00:01:11.069 --> 00:01:15.339
commitment in terms of both personnel and financial resources

22
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.269
to gain this commitment.

23
00:01:17.279 --> 00:01:21.419
Organizational support for business continuity planning efforts must

24
00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:25.569
be provided by executive management or an executive sponsor

25
00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:27.599
without the proper support,

26
00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:31.370
business continuity planning efforts have little chance of success.